  {
    "@id": "https://www.langenburgarts.ca/event-details/blu-beach-band",
    "http://ogp.me/ns#title": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Blu Beach Band"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Hailing from small-town southeast Saskatchewan, Blu Beach Band is a 4-piece ensemble that exudes passion-fuelled coming-of-age energy. This indie-rock group, consisting of Carter Vosper (vocals &amp; guitar), Remi Berthelet (guitar), Eric Vosper (bass) and Riley Buchberger (drums), have been jamming together since their pre-teen days. Now, Blu Beach Band have cranked it up to 11 and transformed their part-time hobby into a full-fledged musical venture. In the past year alone they have played at over 30 venues and shows, including a 16 show summer long tour of Saskatchewan to promote their new EP “A Dog’s Breakfast” released on June 4th.</p>\n<p>Blu Beach Band draws inspiration from an eclectic mix of artists, ranging from Mac Demarco, The Black Keys, Vulfpeck to A Tribe Called Quest. The group’s dazed-and-confused tone, paired with their energetic sunny vibes, will get any crowd up on their feet. The band has proven their ability to rock a wide array of stages; from Music Festivals to theatres to rock clubs; and have opened for Canadian legends Trooper and Streetheart, and most recently Prism.</p>\n<p>Blu Beach Band is currently based out of Regina, SK and are working hard to release a full length Album in 2023 followed by an extensive tour.</p>"
      }
    ],
